<title>SPAIN: Peseta debt/interbank closing report.</title>
<headline>Peseta debt/interbank closing report.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1997-05-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Spanish government bonds ended flat on Wednesday, running out of steam following recent gains and after fresh supply in the shape of Treasury bills and bonds, dealers said.</p>
<p>Bond futures were sustained by buying every time prices dipped, a sign of underlying optimism in the market, a dealer said.</p>
<p>&quot;The market is strong and despite today's auctions. We've still managed to largely ignore weakness in Bunds,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>Yields on five and 15-year bonds, as well as six-month bills fell sharply at today's auction, amid strong demand.</p>
</text>
